Z||000001||88 Fiero||09-24-1999||09:15 PM||||Ka...I think there is still a brand new '88 Fiero GT left...when they close the Fiero Plant..Pontiac raffled 2 1988 Fiero GT..both cars are red...To my understanding both guys who won the car took the car home on a flat bed and wrap the car up...I believe it's for sale last time I remember they were selling it around $50,000 because it's a special Fiero. They have the signatures of all the auto workers who build the car... Fiero Phil of FOCOA got a 1988 Yellow Formula where he monitored this car in the Assembly Plant and have the signatures of all the workers who assembled it....||||reg||1
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||09-25-1999||02:13 AM||||I know of a <B>BRAND NEW</B> 88GT if you are serious about it. It is white on grey interior with sunroof and spoiler and black inset wheels and a 5 speed. The car had 3,048 miles on it last time I saw it(about a year ago) and has never been titled or resistered. The local Pontiac dealer kept the last one it got in and the owner stored it away. There is no price on it, but on the dash is a paper that reads "This is a rare car and deserves a rare price!" I heard that the owner turned down $23,000!!!<P>When I win the lottery, it will be mine!!!<BR>SCCA FIERO &lt;---<B>DREAMER</B>||||reg||14
Z||000003||FieroGT||09-27-1999||03:07 PM||||As if there aren't enough "new" Fieros out there......<P>I saw a website that had an '84 Indy with less than 100 miles on it. It too was for sale. I forget how much the asking price was, but it was steep! The car still had the plastic wrap around the seats, door panels, and steering wheel. A new Fiero as delivered, without even having the dealer prep! Now if I hit the lottery too.......||||reg||1
Z||000004||RFMike||09-28-1999||07:45 PM||||Don,<BR>I'm a little slow responding, I've been on the road, and I'm catching up on posts.  <BR>Do you ever get looks from kids when you drive?  In my work, I drive to high schools, and I get one of two types of looks.  One is, "What is that cool car your driving?"  The other is, "When are you going to grow up?"  Believe it or not, I get the second one more from teachers than kids.  When I'm anywhere near the towns I'm going to, I always drive as a professional, as I'm representing the company I work for, so its not my driving.<BR>I don't really let it bother me, I just find it curious that some people think its not ok for a guy my age to drive a sports car.  That's why I ask, since you have 20 years on me.||||reg||1
